==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-on one's own.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Prepositional phrase===
{{en-PP}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} [[alone|Alone]]; [[by oneself]]; without the [[companionship]] or [[assistance]] of others.
#: {{ux|en|A seven-year-old can get dressed '''on his own''', but it might take a long time.}}
#: {{ux|en|I love cheese on toast, but I won't eat cheese '''on its own'''.}}
#* '''1966''', [[w:Vicki Wickham|Vicki Wickham]], [[w:Simon Napier-Bell|Simon Napier-Bell]] (English lyrics), [[w:Dusty Springfield|Dusty Springfield]] (vocalist), ''[[w:You Don't Have to Say You Love Me|You Don't Have to Say You Love Me]]'', 1965, [[w:Pino Donaggio|Pino Donaggio]], [[w:Vito Pallavicini|Vito Pallavicini]], ''Io che non vivo (senza te)'',
#*: Don't you see / That now you've gone, / And I'm left here '''on my own''', / I will have to follow you / And beg you to come home.
#* {{quote-text|en|date=May 13 2004|author=James B. Hull|title=s:Oversight Hearing on Firefighting Preparedness
|passage=Private operators, for the most part have done an admirable job of keeping these aging aircraft flying, but FAA has essentially said, “It’s public-use aircraft. You’re '''on your own'''.”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008|author=Barbara M. Newman; Philip R. Newman|title=Development Through Life: A Psychosocial Approach|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=FqwzGlvU_1EC&pg=PA215&dq=%22on+their+own%22+-intitle:%22on+-their+-own%22&hl=en&ei=MsglTqSyMMLgmAXSirHcCQ&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=7&ved=0CEgQ6AEwBg#v=onepage&q=%22on%20their%20own%22%20-intitle%3A%22on%20-their%20-own%22&f=false|page=215
|passage=They may adamantly reject help and insist that they can manage '''on their own'''.}}

